    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS, 2 tests, 0 failures \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` rule \u2014 `EMAIL` when an owner has an email, otherwise `PHONE` \u2014 as a derived, read-only field on the owner response, following the same pattern the codebase already uses for `locality` and `membershipLevel`:\n\n1. **`model/ContactPreference.java`** (new) \u2014 a small derivation helper with a static `of(Owner)` returning `\"EMAIL\"` if the owner's email is non-null/non-empty, else `\"PHONE\"`.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field/getter/setter).\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression wiring `contactPreference` to `ContactPreference.of(owner)`.\n\nThe field flows out through the existing `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` path used by `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}`, so both new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) pass with no endpoint/YAML changes needed.",
